    <string name="help_h_area">"Search scope"</string>
    <string name="help_b_area">"The '🔎 Search in' dropdown sets WHERE to search:\n• Everything (name + content) – file names AND file contents at once (default).\n• Folder names – only the names of folders.\n• File names – only the names of files.\n• File content – the text inside books, PDFs, Office documents, etc."</string>
    <string name="help_h_options">"Options (checkboxes)"</string>
    <string name="help_b_options">"• Match case – 'House' then no longer finds 'house'. Default: off.\n• Search across paragraphs – word sequences and the star may cross paragraph breaks. Only for file content.\n• Limit the star's range – the star inside quotes skips at most ~500 characters. Only for file content."</string>
    <string name="help_h_terms">"Entering search terms"</string>
    <string name="help_b_terms">"• One word = the WHOLE word. 'red' finds 'red', but not 'redder' or 'bred'.\n• Star inside a word: 'red*' (starts with red), '*red' (ends with red), 'r*d' (starts r, ends d).\n• Several words with spaces = a fixed sequence, one directly after another: 'good morning' finds only 'good morning', not 'morning … good'.\n• Two words that must BOTH appear (anywhere): put each in double quotes – \"dog\" \"cat\".\n• \"…\" is a phrase; a star inside it skips word boundaries: \"red*light\".\n• A minus excludes: 'novel -fantasy' finds novels WITHOUT 'fantasy'."</string>
    <string name="help_h_categories">"Show / hide categories"</string>
    <string name="help_b_categories">"The blue toggles (files, images, videos, music, contacts, events, SMS, calls, notifications) hide or show a result type."</string>
    <string name="help_h_narrow">"Narrowing &amp; searching further"</string>
    <string name="help_b_narrow">"• '📁 Search in folder…' limits the search to one folder.\n• After a search, 'Search further within these N results' narrows the result (repeatable).\n• Tap a hit = open it. Tap a folder hit = narrow into that folder."</string>
    <string name="help_h_hits">"Matches"</string>
    <string name="help_b_hits">"In content search, the matched words are highlighted in colour and framed with »…« in the text excerpt."</string>
