    <string name="msg_durchsucht_dateinamen_und_in">"Searches file names AND contents (text, Office, PDF, e-books, comic metadata) as well as contacts/events. First, access must be granted and at least one folder chosen."</string>
    <string name="msg_anderen_ordner_hinzufugen">"+ Add another folder"</string>
    <string name="msg_an_der_volltext_eines_archiv">"On: an archive's full text also includes the texts of the documents inside it (PDF, Office, e-books …) – so you can find an archive by its content. Supported: ZIP, 7z, TAR (also .gz/.bz2/.xz) and single compressed files (e.g. report.pdf.gz). RAR by name only (there is no free, GPL-compatible RAR extractor) – to find RAR contents, repack the archive once as ZIP or 7z. Noticeably slower to index, because every contained document is unpacked and read individually. Only in folders with \"content searchable\"."</string>
    <string name="msg_an_vorschaubilder_liegen_im_">"On: thumbnails live in the app's internal storage and persist (count as app data). Off: they live in the cache and may be evicted under storage pressure (regenerated on demand). Not in the database – the backup stays small."</string>
    <string name="msg_diese_datei_en_haben_den_ind">"These file(s) made the indexer hang and are now captured by name only (no content/cover image). Release again via ✕ if you want to retry."</string>
    <string name="msg_was_der_indizierer_zuletzt_g">"What the indexer did last and which files it choked on – helps with troubleshooting. Newest entries on top."</string>
    <string name="msg_eigenstandige_volltextsuche_">"A standalone full-text search over files (text, Office, PDF, e-books, comic metadata), contacts, events and captured notifications. Originally created as a card in EdgeTab."</string>
    <string name="msg_gnu_general_public_license_v">"GNU General Public License v3 (or later). Copyright (c) 2026 Mathias Herbers. Full license text: LICENSE in the source repository.\n\nIncludes third-party libraries each under its own open-source license (combinable with GPLv3): Apache POI, PDFBox-Android, Apache Commons (Collections, Compress, IO, Math), Apache Log4j API and SparseBitSet (all Apache License 2.0), plus curvesapi (BSD license). Full license texts are included with the respective library files."</string>
    <string name="msg_welche_apps_benachrichtigung">"Which apps' notifications should be searchable (only what came through as a notification, no full history):"</string>
    <string name="msg_fur_office_dokumente_gibt_es">"There is no page preview for Office documents (that would mean rebuilding Word/Excel/PowerPoint's own layout engine) – only the cover page shown above, if the file saved one."</string>
